---
/**
 * /check-in — PointCast's daily ping. "Tower, check." and a one-tap answer.
 *
 * The ping is one shared service for the whole network, run from elsegundo.xyz
 * (hello-token-reserve, netlify/functions/ping.mjs, docs/PING-NETWORK.md). This
 * page embeds its widget with site "pointcast", so the call is in PointCast's
 * voice and every answer counts toward the network's 100 check-ins a week.
 * Identity is a browser key (a "line") kept in this origin's localStorage; no
 * account, no cookie, nothing sent out. The widget posts cross-origin to
 * https://elsegundo.xyz/api/v1/ping, which allows pointcast.xyz by name.
 *
 * noindex until the service's PointCast call is live in production and this
 * page is registered in agent-surfaces and llms.txt (follow-up in the doc).
 */
import BlockLayout from '../layouts/BlockLayout.astro';

const title = 'Check in · the PointCast ping';
const description =
  'Tower, check. One tap a day says you are on the air. A streak, a code and a count across the network. No account, no prizes, nothing sent to you unless you ask.';
const service = 'https://elsegundo.xyz';
---

<BlockLayout title={title} description={description} noindex hideAds jsonLd={null}>
  <main class="ci">
    <header class="ci-head">
      <p class="ci-kicker">The ping · PointCast</p>
      <h1>Tower, check.</h1>
      <p class="ci-lede">
        A daily call and response shared by El Segundo, PointCast, Industry Next and the University. Answer today's call in
        PointCast's voice and your line stays on the air. One line, one streak, one count for the whole network.
      </p>
    </header>

    <section class="ci-widget" aria-label="Today's call">
      <div data-ping-site="pointcast" data-ping-voice="broadcast">
        <noscript>
          <p>
            The ping needs JavaScript. You can still read today's call at
            <a href={`${service}/api/v1/ping?site=pointcast`}>{service}/api/v1/ping?site=pointcast</a>.
          </p>
        </noscript>
      </div>
      <script src={`${service}/ping/embed.js`} async></script>
    </section>

    <section class="ci-notes">
      <h2>How it works</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>The call changes at midnight Los Angeles time. Pick the response that answers it.</li>
        <li>Your browser keeps a line and a key. The key never leaves this device; the service stores only a hash.</li>
        <li>Streak titles, no prizes. Ping-backs land in your line inbox only if you opt in.</li>
        <li>
          Bots are welcome: read <a href={`${service}/ping/agents.txt`}>the agents guide</a> and ping with
          <code>"site": "pointcast"</code>.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <h2>Check in from anywhere, and subscribe</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>On any other PointCast page, the small check-in card offers "Checking in from somewhere else": a town or ZIP, and a postmark with the local time, weather, tide and sunset.</li>
        <li>Every check-in across the network: <a href={`${service}/checkins/`}>{service}/checkins/</a>. PointCast only, as <a href={`${service}/api/v1/stamps/feed.json?site=pointcast`}>JSON Feed</a> or <a href={`${service}/api/v1/stamps/feed.xml?site=pointcast`}>Atom</a>.</li>
        <li>The open format behind it: <a href="/check-in/format/">Here, draft 0.1</a>.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="ci-fine">
        Service and rules: <a href={`${service}/ping/`}>{service}/ping/</a>. Not an official City of El Segundo service.
      </p>
    </section>
  </main>
</BlockLayout>

<style>
  .ci { max-width: 40rem; margin: 0 auto; padding: 16px; }
  .ci-kicker { font: 400 12px/1.4 var(--pc-font-mono, ui-monospace, monospace); letter-spacing: 0.06em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--pc-ink-muted, #666); margin: 0 0 4px; }
  .ci h1 { font-size: clamp(28px, 7vw, 40px); line-height: 1.1; margin: 0 0 12px; }
  .ci-lede { font-size: 17px; line-height: 1.45; color: var(--pc-ink-soft, #333); margin: 0 0 20px; }
  .ci-widget { margin: 0 0 28px; --ping-ink: var(--pc-ink, #111); --ping-bg: var(--pc-bg, #fff); --ping-accent: var(--pc-accent, #1028dc); --ping-font: var(--pc-font-sans, system-ui, sans-serif); }
  .ci-notes h2 { font-size: 18px; margin: 0 0 8px; }
  .ci-notes ul { padding-left: 18px; line-height: 1.5; }
  .ci-notes li { margin: 0 0 6px; }
  .ci-fine { font: 400 12px/1.5 var(--pc-font-mono, ui-monospace, monospace); color: var(--pc-ink-muted, #666); }
  code { font: 400 0.95em var(--pc-font-mono, ui-monospace, monospace); }
</style>
